alled "},{"code":"PKAddPaymentPassViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; this class will help you implement that class’ delegate methods. Note that this flow requires a special entitlement from Apple; for more information please see https:\/\/stripe.com\/docs\/issuing\/cards\/digital-wallets .","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.stripe.stripe-issuing-push-provision\/documentation\/StripeIssuing\/STPPushProvisioningContext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"STPPushProvisioningContext","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://com.stripe.stripe-issuing-push-provision/documentation/StripeIssuing/STPFakeAddPaymentPassViewController":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.stripe.stripe-issuing-push-provision\/documentation\/StripeIssuing\/STPFakeAddPaymentPassViewController","title":"STPFakeAddPaymentPassViewController","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"This class is a piece of fake UI that is intended to mimic ","type":"text"},{"code":"PKAddPaymentPassViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". That class is restricted to apps with a special entitlement from Apple, and as such can be difficult to build and test against. This class implements the same public API as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PKAddPaymentPassViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and can be used to develop against the Stripe API in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"testmode only","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". (Obviously it will not actually place cards into the user’s Apple Pay wallet either.) When it’s time to go to production, you may simply replace all references to ","type":"text"},{"code":"STPFakeAddPaymentPassViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your app with ","type":"text"},{"code":"PKAddPaymentPassViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and it will continue to function. For more information on developing against this API, please see https:\/\/stripe.com\/docs\/issuing\/cards\/digital-wallets .","type"